cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Daedalus Engineering AI
message: >-
  If you refer to this software, please cite it using the metadata below.
  Note that every result it produces is simulated and none has been
  physically validated.
type: software
authors:
  - name: LeeSeongmin
    alias: SeongminJaden
repository-code: https://github.com/SeongminJaden/daedalus-engineering-ai
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-09-01'
keywords:
  - engineering design automation
  - finite element method
  - topology optimization
  - multibody dynamics
  - gpu computing
abstract: >-
  An autonomous engineering design engine covering reasoning, design
  generation, GPU accelerated physics, optimization, and an evidence graded
  memory that records how far each result has earned trust. Structural,
  thermal, fluid and multibody analysis are cross validated against
  independently written solvers, specifically CalculiX, OpenFOAM, Pinocchio
  and Gmsh. All results are simulated. Nothing has been built, loaded or
  measured, so the evidence ladder cannot reach its experimentally validated
  level, and the tool is not qualified for certification or production parts.
